# Evidence: the junit report and the witness links

You ship two files under `{{ test_output_dirname }}/` at the repository root:

- `{{ test_output_dirname }}/{{ junit_filename }}`, the junit report of the
  test run described above. Run pytest from the repository root and keep
  `--rootdir=.`:

      mkdir -p {{ test_output_dirname }}
      {{ junit_command_prefix }} <node ids and test modules>

  The repository's pytest configuration already sets
  `junit_family = "xunit1"`; do not change or override it. Everything the run
  must cover goes into one final invocation, after your last commit. A
  failure or error anywhere in the report fails the `junit` gate, and so does
  a required test that is absent or skipped.

- `{{ test_output_dirname }}/{{ witness_links_filename }}`, every `witnesses`
  marker under the test roots, harvested by a collect-only pass with the
  witness collection plugin from the repository root after your last commit:

      {{ harvest_command }}

  A marker whose coordinate names no unit is a broken link and fails the
  `links` gate, and every unit reported with a verdict other than `NONE` must
  have at least one link.
